        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Hanoi</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1010 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">In 1010 the first Lý emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-thai-to">Lý Thái Tổ</a>, moved the capital of Đại Việt to the site of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dai-la">Đại La</a> Citadel and named the city <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a>; a fortified settlement had stood at the centre of what later became Hanoi since the middle of the fifth century CE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the Red River in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, in a region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monsoon">monsoon</a>-influenced humid subtropical climate with four seasons.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a>, capital of Đại Việt from 1010; the Temple of Literature; the Old Quarter and its 36 streets; the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">French Indochina</a> from 1902; the capital of the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>; the capital of unified Vietnam from 1976</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Hanoi is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and its second most populous centrally governed city.</span></div>
